<header class="top"><nav class="wrap mast"><div class="brand">✦ The curious reader’s cabinet / No. 01</div><a href="index.php">← All experiments</a></nav><div class="wrap hero"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow">An experiment in the weight of words</div><h1>The <em>Wordweight</em> Weighhouse</h1><p class="intro">How big is a Bible beside the Summa? Put three extraordinary books on an imaginary scale and watch the numbers find their balance.</p><a class="start" href="#bench">Enter the weighhouse ↓</a></div><figure><img src="wordweight-balance.webp" alt="An original illustration of a brass balance scale in a richly coloured library"><figcaption>ILLUSTRATED FOR THE WEIGHHOUSE · 2026</figcaption></figure></div></header>
<main><section class="wrap section" id="bench"><div class="heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / The balance</div><h2>What tips the scale?</h2></div><p>Add up to five copies of any book to either pan. Here, a word is a unit of weight. No heavy lifting required.</p></div><div class="workshop"><div class="bench"><div class="scale-head"><strong>Books on the brass</strong><span>WORD COUNTS · NOT PHYSICAL MASS</span></div><div class="scale" role="img" id="scaleGraphic" aria-label="Empty balance scale"><div class="post"></div><div class="beam" id="beam"><div class="pan left"><div class="pile" id="leftPile">◇</div></div><div class="pan right"><div class="pile" id="rightPile">◇</div></div></div></div><div class="balance-status" id="status" aria-live="polite">The pans are waiting.<small>Add a book to begin.</small></div><div class="sides" id="sides"></div></div><aside class="guide"><div class="eyebrow">Reference card</div><h3>The three volumes</h3><p>Word counts from Jon’s 2011 comparison. Edition and counting methods matter; treat these as an illuminating approximation, not a universal constant.</p><?php foreach ($books as $book): ?><div class="fact"><span><?= htmlspecialchars($book['name']) ?></span><strong><?= number_format($book['words']) ?></strong></div><?php endforeach; ?><p class="note">A curious near-balance: 2 Bibles + 2 Catechisms versus 1 Summa. Can you get closer?</p><button class="reset" id="reset" type="button">Clear both pans ↺</button></aside></div></section>
<section class="challenge"><div class="wrap challenge-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / A second way to weigh them</div><h2>Turn words into evenings.</h2><p>Set a comfortable daily reading budget. Watch the books stretch or shrink into days, with no suggestion that reading a theology classic should become a speedrun.</p><p class="footnote" style="color:#b9aba0">One “day” here means your chosen number of words read. The estimate excludes reflection, study and rereading.</p></div><div class="dial"><label for="daily">Words per reading day</label><div class="number"><output id="budget">2,000</output> <span>words</span></div><input id="daily" type="range" min="500" max="10000" step="250" value="2000"><div class="dial-result" id="readout" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div></section>
<footer class="wrap source"><div class="eyebrow">The spark behind the experiment</div><p>Inspired by Jon’s <a href="https://cooltoolsforcatholics.blogspot.com/2011/02/relative-lengths-of-bible-summa-and.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">“Relative lengths of the Bible, the Summa, and the Catechism”</a>. I loved the way three plain numbers suddenly make a whole library feel different.</p><div class="footnote">Made for curious readers · Counts: Bible (Douay-Rheims) 1,063,100 · Summa Theologica 2,569,567 · Catechism 227,929</div></footer></main>
<script>
const books = <?= json_encode($books, JSON_HEX_TAG|JSON_HEX_AMP|JSON_HEX_APOS|JSON_HEX_QUOT) ?>;
const state = [[0,0,0],[0,0,0]];
const names = ['Left pan','Right pan'];
const fmt = n => new Intl.NumberFormat('en-CA').format(n);
const sides = document.getElementById('sides');
function makeControls(){ sides.innerHTML = names.map((name,s)=>'<div class="side"><div class="side-title">'+name+' <b id="total'+s+'">0 words</b></div>'+books.map((book,i)=>'<div class="row"><span class="name">'+book.short+'</span><button type="button" data-s="'+s+'" data-i="'+i+'" data-step="-1" aria-label="Remove '+book.short+' from '+name+'">−</button><output id="count'+s+i+'">0</output><button type="button" data-s="'+s+'" data-i="'+i+'" data-step="1" aria-label="Add '+book.short+' to '+name+'">+</button></div>').join('')+'</div>').join(''); }
function render(){const totals=state.map(row=>row.reduce((sum,n,i)=>sum+n*books[i].words,0)); state.forEach((row,s)=>{row.forEach((n,i)=>document.getElementById('count'+s+i).textContent=n);document.getElementById('total'+s).textContent=fmt(totals[s])+' words';document.getElementById((s?'right':'left')+'Pile').textContent=row.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)?'▰'.repeat(Math.min(4,row.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0))):'◇'});const diff=totals[0]-totals[1];const tilt=totals[0]+totals[1]===0?0:Math.max(-13,Math.min(13,-diff/Math.max(...totals)*13));document.getElementById('beam').style.setProperty('--tilt',tilt+'deg');let message,detail;if(!totals[0]&&!totals[1]){message='The pans are waiting.';detail='Add a book to begin.'}else if(!diff){message='A perfect balance!';detail=fmt(totals[0])+' words on each side.'}else{const heavier=diff>0?'Left':'Right';const difference=Math.abs(diff);message=heavier+' pan is heavier.';detail='By '+fmt(difference)+' word'+(difference===1?'':'s')+'.'+(difference<30000&&totals[0]&&totals[1]?' Astonishingly close!':'')}document.getElementById('status').innerHTML=message+'<small>'+detail+'</small>';document.getElementById('scaleGraphic').setAttribute('aria-label',message+' '+detail)}
sides.addEventListener('click',e=>{const b=e.target.closest('button[data-step]');if(!b)return;const s=Number(b.dataset.s),i=Number(b.dataset.i),step=Number(b.dataset.step);state[s][i]=Math.max(0,Math.min(5,state[s][i]+step));render()});document.getElementById('reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{state.forEach(row=>row.fill(0));render()});makeControls();render();
const daily=document.getElementById('daily');function updateDaily(){const n=Number(daily.value);document.getElementById('budget').textContent=fmt(n);document.getElementById('readout').innerHTML=books.map(book=>'<div><strong>'+fmt(Math.ceil(book.words/n))+'</strong> reading days for the '+book.short+'</div>').join('')}daily.addEventListener('input',updateDaily);updateDaily();
</script></body></html>
